## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical experience designing observable, scalable Azure telemetry pipelines with proper instrumentation, tenant isolation, and comprehensive monitoring integration for enterprise-grade media analytics platforms.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry integration across Event Hubs, Databricks, and Delta Lake
- End-to-end trace correlation and structured logging
- Adaptive sampling strategies and retention policies
- Tenant-level RBAC and data governance
- Comprehensive monitoring with Application Insights and Azure Monitor
- Real-time alerting and SLA management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Propagate correlation across services
const traceHeader = appInsights.getCorrelationContext();
const traceId = traceHeader.traceId;

// Instrument Event Hubs producer
eventHubProducer.send({
  body: eventData,
  properties: {
    traceId: traceId,
    tenantId: tenantId,
    region: region,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  }
});

// Configure OpenTelemetry sampling
const sampler = new ParentBasedSampler({
  root: new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.01) // 1% production
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical Azure-native data path design, governance, and cost controls for a multi-tenant SaaS.

## Key Concepts
- REST ingestion with serverless compute (Azure Functions)
- ADLS Gen2 with tenant-prefixed folders for per-tenant isolation
- Data Factory for hourly pipeline orchestration
- Purview for data governance and lineage tracking
- Synapse for analytics and Azure ML for anomaly detection
- Paired region DR and budget-based controls for data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to trigger Data Factory pipeline on schedule
export default async function (context, req) {
    const pipelineRunner = await context.executionContext.getBindingData();

    const response = await fetch('https://management.azure.com/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{rg}/providers/Microsoft.DataFactory/factories/{df}/pipelines/WeatherIngestionPipeline/createRun?api-version=2018-06-01', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.ARM_TOKEN}`,
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        }
    });

    context.log('Pipeline triggered:', response.status);
